  "intro": "Nashville is a broadcast town before it is anything else. The FM dial is denser and better engineered than almost any market its size, WSM’s clear-channel AM signal has been reaching half the country at night since 1925, and the medium wave band here after dark is genuinely worth sitting through. Beyond the transmitters, the metro sprawls across rolling limestone country with no single dominant high point, so repeater coverage is patchy in a way that makes local knowledge matter.",
  "introz": "纳什维尔首先是一座广播之城。它的调频频段比同等规模市场都更密、工程水平更高；WSM 的清频中波自 1925 年起入夜就能覆盖半个美国，天黑后这里的中波频段真的值得坐下来慢慢听。除了发射台之外，都会区铺展在起伏的石灰岩地形上，没有一个绝对制高点，所以中继覆盖是零碎的——这让本地经验变得重要。",
